361 - Hark! 'Tis the Shepherd's Voice I Hear
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 361
Topic: Christian Church - 

Verse 1:
[G]Hark! 'tis the Shepherd's voice [D]I hear,
[D7]Out in the desert [G]dark and drear,
[G]Calling the sheep [C]who've [Am]gone [Bm]astray,
[G/D]Far from [D7]the [G]Shepherd's fold away.

Refrain:
[C]Bring them [G]in, Bring them in,
[D]Bring them [Am]in [D]from [G]the fields of sin;
[C]Bring them in, Bring them in,
[G]Bring the wanderers to [D7]Jesus.

Verse 2:
[G]Who'll go and help the Shepherd [D]kind,
[D7]Help Him the wandering ones [G]to find?
[G]Who'll bring them back [C]into [Bm]the [G/D]fold,
[G/D]Where they'll [D7]be [G]sheltered from the cold?

Verse 3:
[G]Out in the desert hear [D]their cry,
[D7]Out on the mountain [G]wild and high,
[G]Hark! 'tis the Master [Am]speaks [Bm]to [G/D]thee,
[G/D]"Go, find [D7]My [G]sheep where 'er they be."
